From: Ilya I. Nikitin <ilya.i.nikitin@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pulse: ignore compressed ALSA cards for call routing

PipeWire exposes compressed-offload devices with the same UCM ports as
the PCM sound card. Selecting that duplicate leaves callaudiod without
a usable PCM sink or microphone. Ignore compressed devices before card
selection, while retaining PulseAudio cards without a device.api property.

---
--- a/src/cad-pulse.c
+++ b/src/cad-pulse.c
@@ -465,6 +465,10 @@
         return;
     }
 
+    prop = pa_proplist_gets(info->proplist, "device.api");
+    if (g_strcmp0(prop, "alsa:compressed") == 0)
+        return;
+
     prop = pa_proplist_gets(info->proplist, "alsa.card_name");
     g_debug("CARD: prop %s = %s", "alsa.card_name", prop);
     if (prop && g_str_has_prefix(prop, CARD_MODEM_NAME))
